From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Install/Linux: skip ly_copy lrelease rpath-change under system Qt6

Companion to Patch0017. That patch handled the POST_BUILD lrelease
rpath-patch in LmbrCentral's lrelease_linux.cmake; this one handles the
SECOND place lrelease's rpath is rewritten -- the %install-time ly_copy in
cmake/Platform/Linux/Install_linux.cmake, which copies runtime dependencies
into the install tree and rewrites lrelease's RPATH from $ORIGIN/../lib to
$ORIGIN.

Under the Fedora system-Qt6 swap the deployed lrelease is Fedora's
qt6-qttools binary with no RPATH/RUNPATH (it resolves Qt via the default
/usr/lib64 loader search), so file(RPATH_CHANGE) aborts at install:

  CMake Error at build/cmake_install.cmake:23083 (file):
    file RPATH_CHANGE could not write new RPATH: $ORIGIN to the file
    .../opt/O3DE/26.05.0/bin/Linux/profile/Default/./lrelease
    No valid ELF RPATH or RUNPATH entry exists in the file;

Setting $ORIGIN would be wrong anyway -- it would point the loader at the
install bin dir instead of /usr/lib64 where the system Qt libs live. Skip
the rewrite; the copied lrelease keeps no rpath, finds Qt via /usr/lib64,
and passes check-rpaths cleanly.

Caught on the first fully-compiling system_qt6 build (COPR 10858337,
fedora-44, 2026-08-13) at %install, after profile [3263/3263] AND monolithic
[871/871] both linked against system Qt 6.11.1. system_qt6-only.

Signed-off-by: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
---
--- a/cmake/Platform/Linux/Install_linux.cmake
+++ b/cmake/Platform/Linux/Install_linux.cmake
@@ -40,7 +40,10 @@
                     execute_process(COMMAND @CMAKE_STRIP@ "${target_file}")
                 endif()
             elseif("${source_file}" MATCHES "lrelease")
-                file(RPATH_CHANGE FILE "${target_file}" OLD_RPATH "\$ORIGIN/../lib" NEW_RPATH "\$ORIGIN")
+                # system Qt6 swap: the deployed lrelease is Fedora's qt6-qttools binary
+                # with no rpath (it finds Qt via /usr/lib64). Skip the $ORIGIN rpath-change:
+                # file(RPATH_CHANGE) fatally errors with no OLD_RPATH to match, and $ORIGIN
+                # would misdirect the loader away from the system Qt libraries.
             endif()
         endif()
     endforeach()
